==Enemy==
Oldstrich is by far one of the deadliest ostriches in the game. This husk of a comedian is even stronger and more relentless of a pusher than a 300% [[R.Ost]], having considerably higher stats, more speed, only 4 knockbacks, and 300 range to hit most non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] [[:Category:Zombie Killer Cats|Zombie Killers]], with none of the drawbacks that make [[M. Ost]] less of a threat. To counter tankers and specialist meatshields like [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]], he also comes with a 20% chance to deal 20% Toxic damage on every attack to melt anything he can't overwhelm with raw damage. Combined with his 70% resistance to all debuffs and infinite revives if not Zombie-Killed, Oldstrich will tear through your defense if not swiftly dispatched.

==Strategy==
This feathered fiend's long range and fast attacks make most non-Uber anti-Zombie units ineffective, while most [[:Category:Cats with Toxic Immunity|Toxic-immune units]] will not be able to permanently kill it due to lacking Zombie Killer. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Archer Cat (Rare Cat)|Cataur]] are some of the only non-Uber Zombie Killers that can outrange it, making them good options even with Oldstrich being able to shrug off Housewife's Slow. A combination of [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] to stall it and [[Bakery Cat (Rare Cat)|Fried Chicken Cat]] to disable its Toxic ability with Curse can hold it in place, although a stack of Fried Chicken Cats are needed to maintain full uptime, and the duo may struggle if it comes with other traited enemies. Likewise, a stack of Talented [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocats]] can assist with their Slow and Weaken Talents, though they do not have Zombie Killer. [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] is a great option against Oldstrich, being Strong against Zombies with Toxic Immunity, allowing him to potentially land one or two attacks.

A high level Holy Blast can be used to chip at Oldstrich or even Z-Kill it, albeit requiring some guessing to estimate when it's low enough for the final blow. A Level 30 Holy Blast will deal 15% of its HP, meaning that it'll be able to kill it slightly after its third knockback at 25% HP, with a few more moments of attacking to deal the remaining 10% damage.

