==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Da Chōrō (ダ・チョー老), may be a pun on 駝鳥 ''dachō'' (ostrich), 超 ''chō'' (super), 老 ''rō'' (old age), 長老 ''chōrō'' (an elder) and possibly the Italian musical term ''[[wikipedia:Da capo|da capo]]'' ("from the beginning").
**The "Da" may also be a reference to Italian polymath [[wikipedia:Leonardo da Vinci|Leonardo da Vinci]]. Da Vinci was a pioneering anatomist who dissected more than 30 human corpses and extensively studied the skeletal structures, muscles and organs of both humans and other vertebrates, including birds, which may play into Oldstrich's [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombie]] trait. His Toxic ability could allude to how da Vinci [https://www.acs.org/pressroom/presspacs/2023/october/mona-lisa-hides-a-surprising-mix-of-toxic-pigments.html used toxic pigments] when painting the ''[[wikipedia:Mona Lisa|Mona Lisa]]'', while his Japanese description mentions him losing his emotions, which could reference da Vinci's fascination with emotions and attempts to identify their source, and gaining knowledge of all kinds of comedy, just as da Vinci was versed in many fields of knowledge.
*Oldstrich's skeletal structure differs greatly from [https://bmcvetres.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s12917-023-03665-6/figures/1 that of an actual ostrich].
*Oldstrich and [[Casaurian Darkjo]] are the only enemies with a non-guaranteed [[Toxic]] ability.

